tatus":"published","payload":{"options":[{"id":"a9e1e5e5","text":"8 849 m"},{"id":"d18cabc5","text":"7 546 m"},{"id":"2f55bba8","text":"9 312 m"},{"id":"bf515e0e","text":"8 091 m"}]},"answer":{"option_id":"a9e1e5e5"}},{"external_key":"geo-022","concept_id":"geography.relief.andes_longest","concept_label":"Les Andes","type":"true_false","prompt":"Les Andes sont la plus longue chaîne de montagnes continentale du monde.","explanation":"Les Andes s''étirent sur environ 7 000 km, du Venezuela à la Terre de Feu.","difficulty":45,"status":"published","payload":{},"answer":{"value":true}},{"external_key":"geo-023","concept_id":"geography.oceans.longest_french_river","concept_label":"Plus long fleuve de France","type":"mcq","prompt":"Quel est le plus long fleuve de France ?","explanation":"La Loire mesure environ 1 000 km, entièrement en France. Le Rhône prend sa source en Suisse.","difficulty":35,"status":"published","payload":{"options":[{"id":"b2123d54","text":"La Loire"},{"id":"5043b833","text":"La Seine"},{"id":"c63009d5","text":"Le Rhône"},{"id":"20ce63da","text":"La Garonne"}]},"answer":{"option_id":"b2123d54"}},{"external_key":"geo-024","concept_id":"geography.oceans.largest_ocean","concept_label":"Plus grand océan","type":"mcq","prompt":"Quel est le plus vaste océan du monde ?","explanation":"Le Pacifique couvre environ un tiers de la surface de la Terre, plus que toutes les terres émergées réunies.","difficulty":18,"status":"published","payload":{"options":[{"id":"e9911d86","text":"Pacifique"},{"id":"4ef02ee0","text":"Atlantique"},{"id":"c48545fe","text":"Indien"},{"id":"7d629da2","text":"Arctique"}]},"answer":{"option_id":"e9911d86"}},{"external_key":"geo-025","concept_id":"geography.oceans.rivers_length_order","concept_label":"Longueur des fleuves français","type":"ordering","prompt":"Classe ces fleuves du plus long au plus court (longueur totale).","explanation":"Loire ≈ 1 000 km, Rhône ≈ 810 km (dont une partie en Suisse), Seine ≈ 775 km, Garonne ≈ 530 km.","di